{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-94082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center of the elliptic cone $2(x+2)^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}={z}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+2)^{2}+3(y-1)^{2} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{1/2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{1/3} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{1/2}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{1/3} & =(z-0)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(-2,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-94082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,-1,0)"] ["math" "(-2,1,0)"] ["math" "(0,0,0)"] ["math" "(2,-1,0)"] ["math" "(2,1,0)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-2,1,0)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=(z+3)^{2},$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{4} & =(0+3)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{4}{4} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+1 & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2} & =8 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(-2,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-94081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0)$"] ["text" "$(-2,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(-4,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$"] ["text" "$(2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$"] ["text" "$(4,0,0)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center of the elliptic cone $7{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=21{z}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(x-0)^{2}+3(y-0)^{2} & =21(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{1/7}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{1/3} & =\\frac{(z-0)^{2}}{1/21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(0,0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-94602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-7,-3,-21)"] ["math" "(0,0,0)"] ["math" "(0,0,1)"] ["math" "(3,7,1)"] ["math" "(7,3,21)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,0,0)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2},$ find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\ 0+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $y$-axis is $(0,0,0)$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-94603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,4,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,1.5,0)$ and $(0,4,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,1.5,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,2,0)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,0)$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-176833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x+8)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3}=\\frac{(z-7)^{2}}{7},$ find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-176833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+8)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =\\frac{(0-7)^{2}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{64}{16}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =\\frac{49}{7} \\\\ 4+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{6} & =7 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =3 \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y+5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-5\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-8,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,-2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-176833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-176833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-176833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,-2,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,-2,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,7,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,-8,0)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-176833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,-2,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}={z}^{2}\\,?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $yz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-94486" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94486" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=-\\frac{y}{3}"] ["math" "z=-\\frac{y}{3}\\pm 1"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{9}"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{9}+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94486" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-95462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $(x-1)^{2}+7{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2}\\,?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-95462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+7(0)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}z & =\\pm (x-1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm 4(x-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-95462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-95462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-95462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=-4x+4"] ["math" "z=-\\frac{1}{4}x-1"] ["math" "z=4x+1"] ["math" "z=\\pm 4(x-1)"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x+1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-95462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\pm 4(x-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the trace of the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}={z}^{2}$ and the $xz$-plane are two lines, what is the intersection point of these lines?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x-1}{2} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\frac{x-1}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{1-x}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the point of intersection of both lines, we equate the right-hand sides. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{2} & =\\frac{1-x}{2} \\\\ x-1 & =1-x \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ in the equation of the first line and solving for $z,$ we obtain $z=\\frac{1-1}{2}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(1,0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-35266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,1,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})"] ["math" "(1,0,0)"] ["math" "(3,\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2})"] ["math" "(5,0,2)"] ["math" "(\\sqrt{2}+1,1,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,0,0)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=(z-4)^{2}\\,?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =(z-4)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =(z-4)^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{y}{2} & =z-4 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $yz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-35596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=-\\frac{y}{2}+4"] ["math" "z=\\frac{y}{2}+2"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+2"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4"] ["math" "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{2}}+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-35596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cone $9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=18{z}^{2}\\,?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=18(0)^{2} \\\\ 9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives in the $xy$-plane the point $(2,0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4d1758a8d55d8702d2a7d48777f4dbf76dc2567a9bfb0b88066fe6eb37222d9"} {"question" "q-94496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2,0,0)"] ["math" "(9,2,0)"] ["math" "y=\\pm 3x-5"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2x}{3}+18"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{x}{3}+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "q-94496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2,0,0)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/state.json" "file_sha256" "4ce577af3320d56e3bd3902696c9d0896d337dedd42f61ccbf591973f9181374"} {"question" "e-8216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic cone $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{4} + \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{2} = \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{3},$ find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/example-8216.json" "file_sha256" "3049fd772a0b384d73922cf659f20e46a83a51b012ca456c5221eb0397366a1c"} {"question" "e-8216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $z$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{4}{2} & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 1+2 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 9 & =(z+1)^{2} \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-4,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/example-8216.json" "file_sha256" "3049fd772a0b384d73922cf659f20e46a83a51b012ca456c5221eb0397366a1c"} {"question" "e-8217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $3x^2 +  4y ^2=12(z+3)^2\\: ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/example-8217.json" "file_sha256" "ee3d4489d89a6ec80d8478cf7343fd13425d21b02e94b49f35fa990458880139"} {"question" "e-8217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+4\\cdot {0}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(z+3)^{2} \\\\ \\pm x & =2(z+3) \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x}{2} & =z+3 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{x}{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z = \\pm\\dfrac{x}{2}-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042648/example-8217.json" "file_sha256" "ee3d4489d89a6ec80d8478cf7343fd13425d21b02e94b49f35fa990458880139"}] "usage" {"e-8216" [] "q-94082" [] "q-35596" [] "e-8217" [] "q-94081" []} "basis" 1563 "retractions" [[17592186125155 :question/problem "Find the center of the elliptic cone $2(x + 2)^{2} + 3(y - 1)^{2} = z^{2}$."] [17592186125154 :question/problem "Given the elliptic cone $((x - 2)^{2})/(2) + ((y + 2)^{2})/(4) = (z + 3)^{2}$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis."] [17592186124809 :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = (z - 4)^{2}$?"] [17592186124314 :question/problem "Given the elliptic cone $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{4} + \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{2} = \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{3}$, find its intercepts with the $z$-axis."] [17592186124314 :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((0 - 2)^{2})/(4) + ((0 - 2)^{2})/(2) &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n\\frac{4}{4} + \\frac{4}{2} &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n1 + 2 &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n3 &= ((z + 1)^{2})/(3) \\\\\n9 &= (z + 1)^{2} \\\\\nz + 1 &= ± 3 \\\\\nz &= -1 ± 3 \\\\\nz &= -4, 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2)$."] [17592186124315 :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $3x^2 + 4y ^2=12(z+3)^2\\:$?"] [17592186124315 :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x^{2} + 4 \\cdot 0^{2} &= 12(z + 3)^{2} \\\\\n3x^{2} &= 12(z + 3)^{2} \\\\\nx^{2} &= 4(z + 3)^{2} \\\\\n± x &= 2(z + 3) \\\\\n± \\frac{x}{2} &= z + 3 \\\\\nz &= ± \\frac{x}{2} - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations\n\n$$\nz = \\pm\\dfrac{x}{2}-3\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121877 17592186121878 17592186121879 17592186121880 17592186121881 17592186123947 17592186123948 17592186123949 17592186123950 17592186123951 17592186123953 17592186123954 17592186123955 17592186123956 17592186123957] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121876 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121876 :answer-field/id] [17592186121876 :answer-field/key] [17592186121876 :answer-field/type] [17592186123946 :answer-field/correct] [17592186123946 :answer-field/id] [17592186123946 :answer-field/key] [17592186123946 :answer-field/type] [17592186123952 :answer-field/correct] [17592186123952 :answer-field/id] [17592186123952 :answer-field/key] [17592186123952 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
